      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your empathy for your loved ones stems from how they depend on your survival, yet surviving is not a project but a temporary situation and your exhaustion is valid and justified given your burdens. The \"weight\" they carry is a temporary reality of your illness, not a permanent state of their lives, because they will eventually be taken from those hours of caretaking. Please do not question your existence or your right to exist; their capacity to love you is precisely why they are willing to endure their own grief today so you can live yours.",
